    "ground_truth_policy": "For consequential claims, use the strongest applicable authoritative evidence available: literal governing source for requested semantics, live state for mutable external conditions, current interface/configuration for capability/config facts, and current self-execution records for first-person action provenance. Evidence must be matched to the proposition it actually establishes; external effect evidence cannot substitute for action occurrence and self-execution evidence cannot by itself establish an external effect. For consequential facts, select the source entitled to establish the exact claim. Use live/environmental evidence for current state and required effects; use current self-execution evidence for claims that this executor performed prescribed operations. Do not allow one evidence type to substitute for another claim type.",
    "self_assertion_policy": "Unsupported executor assertion is never sufficient when stronger observable evidence is available or when the claim concerns completion of a prescribed operation. Self-report may summarize evidence already present, but it does not create that evidence. Executor self-assertion is never stronger than the underlying execution/evidence record. A bare assertion does not establish action occurrence, state, or effect when stronger observable evidence is available or required.",
