  "examples_policy": {
    "when_required": [
      "A consequential instruction remains materially ambiguous after definitions/referent repair and a representative example can reduce that ambiguity.",
      "A predictable failure mode is easier to distinguish through a negative or contrastive case than through additional abstract wording alone.",
      "A boundary condition changes behavior and the boundary is likely to be misapplied without an example.",
      "The procedure introduces a locally redefined concept whose practical application would otherwise be uncertain.",
      "A known ambiguity remains likely despite explicit rules and a canonical example materially reduces it.",
      "A boundary between permitted and prohibited behavior is easy to misclassify.",
      "A negative example is needed to distinguish an invalid proxy from valid evidence.",
      "A contrastive example is needed to distinguish two neighboring semantic classes."
