      "negative",
      "contrastive",
      "boundary"
    ],
    "constraints": [
      "Every example must be explicitly labeled as an example and linked to the governing rule it illustrates.",
      "An example must not introduce a consequential rule that is absent from governing semantics.",
      "Example-specific incidental details are non-governing unless a rule explicitly incorporates them.",
      "Examples must be checked for consistency with the governing rule and with each other.",
      "Do not require examples where they add no material disambiguation value.",
      "Examples are illustrative, not independently governing.",
      "Every normative implication intended to govern execution must also appear in explicit rules.",
      "Examples must not freeze implementation choices that the procedure intentionally delegates.",
      "Examples should be minimal and representative rather than exhaustive unless exhaustiveness itself is required.",
      "Where examples conflict with explicit governing semantics, explicit governing semantics control."
